# Task List
// A to-do list:  add a task, check it off, filter the list, and edit the selected tasks together.
// Its tasks are this project's own `<spell-view "task">`;  this file holds their list, and the app.

## The checklist
// The tasks, each its own element inside it:  `<task-list-checklist>`, around its `<task-list-task>`s.

a "checklist" is a viewable list of tasks:
	// What it shows:  every task, the ones still to do, or the ones done
	- its "showing" is one of all, active or done
		- it "is showing (showing)"

	// on the page, its tasks can be dragged to another place:  they move as the pointer does, gliding there
	- its items can be reordered immediately
	// each task, unless the filter hides it
	- to draw each item:
		if it is showing active and the task is done return nothing
		if it is showing done and the task is active return nothing
		return draw the task
	// What it shows while it's empty
	- to draw its placeholder:
		<ui-text part="placeholder">Nothing to do</ui-text>

	- to test the filter:
		set the tasks to a new checklist
		add (a new task with title = "a", done = yes) to the tasks
		add (a new task with title = "b") to the tasks
		the length of (tasks in the tasks where it is active) should be 1
// a task is in one checklist at a time
a task belongs to one checklist

## The app
// Its toolbar, the new task's field, then the list beside the property editor.

task list is an app:
	- its "checklist" is a new checklist
	// The next task's title, as the new task's field holds it
	- its "draft" is text
	- its "active count" is the length of (tasks in its checklist where it is active)

	// A new task list shows every task, and starts with a few
	- to create it:
		set the showing of its checklist to all
		add (a new task with title = "Write the Task List example", priority = high, done = yes) to its checklist
		add (a new task with title = "Teach it to draw", priority = normal) to its checklist
		add (a new task with title = "Select some tasks, then edit them together", priority = normal) to its checklist
		add (a new task with title = "Drag tasks to reorder them", priority = low) to its checklist

	// The draft, as a new task at the end of the list;  the field empties
	- to add the draft:
		if its draft is "" return
		add (a new task with title = its draft, priority = normal) to its checklist
		clear its draft

	// Which tasks the list shows:  the toolbar ticks the one it's showing
	- group "filter"
	- to show all:
		- icon "list"
		- selected when its checklist is showing all
		set the showing of its checklist to all
	- to show to do:
		- icon "square outline"
		- selected when its checklist is showing active
		set the showing of its checklist to active
	- to show done:
		- icon "check square outline"
		- selected when its checklist is showing done
		set the showing of its checklist to done
	- to remove the done tasks:
		- icon "trash alternate outline"
		remove tasks in its checklist where it is done
	- its "tasks menu" is a menu of "show all" , "show to do" , "show done" , "-" and "remove the done tasks"

	// The property editor edits every selected task at once:  a property they disagree on shows Mixed
	- to draw it:
		<ui-container class="TaskList">
			<ui-toolbar menu="tasks menu" aria-label="Tasks">
				<ui-text slot="title" size="large">Task List</ui-text>
				<ui-text slot="right">
					<if its active count is 0>All done<otherwise>{its active count} to do</otherwise>
				</ui-text>
			</ui-toolbar>
			<ui-form value={it}>
				<ui-input name="draft" placeholder="Something to do" aria-label="New task" fluid action>
					<ui-button slot="action" color="primary" disabled={its draft is ""} onClick={add the draft}>Add</ui-button>
				</ui-input>
			</ui-form>
			<ui-grid columns="2" stackable>
				{draw its checklist}
				<ui-property-editor label="Selected tasks" schema="task-list-task" value={the selection of its checklist}>
					<ui-property name="title"/>
					<ui-property name="priority"/>
					<ui-property name="done"/>
					<ui-property name="notes"/>
				</ui-property-editor>
			</ui-grid>
		</ui-container>

start the task list
